164:**8. Medium — ledger 9 appears compatible, but the design names the wrong limits and overstates current acceptance evidence. Focus point 5.**
165:
166:At ledger commit **`a2b30128`**:
167:
168:| Item | Actual source rule | Consequence |
169:|---|---|---|
170:| Public inputs | `MAX_CALL_PUBLIC_INPUTS = 1 << 16` | A source constant, not a `LedgerParameters` field. (`onchain-runtime/src/transcript.rs:87`.) |
171:| Contract operations | `MAX_CONTRACT_OPERATIONS = 256` | Limits operations stored by a contract, not Sherlock execution steps. (`ledger/src/structure.rs:1926`; `ledger/src/verify.rs:1836`.) |
172:| Verifier key bytes | Deserializer rejects a raw VK buffer above 50,000 bytes | This is the relevant explicit VK-size guard. (`transient-crypto/src/proofs.rs:417–435`.) |
173:| Transaction size and costs | `LedgerParameters.limits` contains transaction bytes, block limits and metadata limits | Read actual target parameters; do not substitute source defaults. (`ledger/src/structure.rs:1265–1307`.) |
174:| Initial transaction-byte limit | 1 MiB in `INITIAL_LIMITS` | A default, not evidence of the live network value. (`ledger/src/structure.rs:1283`.) |
175:
176:The manifest’s 2,217-byte tagged decider key and the design’s 70-slot template are comfortably below the cited size/input caps. But the template manifest explicitly says it predates the repin and has an unobserved compiler version. This establishes no full-transaction acceptance result for the final universal-leaf chain. (`qa/sherlock/manifests/sherlock-run-contract.json:2`, `:10–13`; `design.md:91`.)
177:
178:The `VERIFIER_KEY_SIZE = 2875` constant elsewhere in the ledger is an estimated size, not the deserialization cap. It must not become an accidental acceptance rule. (`a2b30128:ledger/src/structure.rs:1922–1924`.)
179:
180:The recorded network observation also contradicts the design’s Preprod status. It reports all three networks on node `2.1.101-913ec011`, spec 2001100 and ledger 9.1.0.1; this is a saved observation, not a live check performed for this review. (`research/midnight-ledger9-20261107/api/rpc-status-20261110.json:2–25`; `design.md:142`.)
181:
182:**Proposed change:** correct SMN-003, recapture the template, measure the complete serialized transaction, and run full call validation against recorded target parameters. Preserve the distinction between local source provenance and observed deployed runtime identity.
183:
184:**Tasks:** 2.1 status reconciliation, 2.5, 5.1 and Preview qualification.
