188:**9. Medium — the GPU adoption argument double-counts work. Additional finding.**
189:
190:The decision record uses `m + q = 0.256 + 0.57 = 0.83`. The profiler explicitly says q overlaps m and that they must not be summed. It defines q from vanishing, quotient, NTT and advice-NTT spans; therefore q is not the fraction directly removable by an FFT implementation. The q value also comes from a different diagnostic run than the main m measurement. (`qa/sherlock/decisions/speed-levers.json:31`, `:67`; `scripts/qa/profile-recursion.py:868–895`.)
191:
192:Using m=0.256 alone gives an **idealized MSM-only speedup ceiling** of `1/(1−0.256) ≈ 1.34×`, before transfer and integration overhead. That estimate cannot rescue an S=1 chain requiring roughly 2.6× faster nodes. (`qa/sherlock/decisions/speed-levers.json:9`; arithmetic in concern 3.)
193:
194:**Proposed change:** base GPU adoption on exclusive, directly offloadable phase shares from one qualified run and measured whole-chain benefit. Keep proof-byte equivalence, CPU fallback and memory accounting. Give the GPU no credit in G-C until measured.
195:
196:**Tasks:** 2.8, 2.10b–2.10f, 4.10 and 5.8.
