198:## 5. Proposed edits to design.md and tasks.md
199:
200:These are proposed text changes only.
201:
202:**A. Replace the scope claim in design §3.6 and clarify SRC-017.**  
203:Affected text: `design.md:116`; `requirements.md:39`.
204:
205:> Sherlock provides recursive proofs of executions of the admitted bounded machine. For fixed rule inventory, carrier layout, bounds, profile and batch size S, the leaf, linear-node and decider keys do not depend on the program, initial state or execution length. The deployed acceptRun instance binds one program and initial-state digest.
206:>
207:> The segment model also describes tree composition. A tree implementation has its own recursive statement and dependent keys. Arbitrary-circuit aggregation is a separate extension requiring authenticated circuit identity, statement adapters and a composition policy.
208:
209:**B. Replace the U/F decision and S gate in design §§3.4–3.5.**  
210:Affected text: `design.md:95`, `:107`, `:110`; `tasks.md:65`, `:68`.
211:
212:> Select the leaf construction and S from measurements of the complete admitted relation and its dependent node and decider. Treat `k_U + log2(S) <= 20` as an initial sizing estimate; confirm actual rows and architecture at each candidate S.
213:>
214:> U remains eligible at k_U=18 if S=4 passes the complete path’s cost and memory gates. F at S=1 is a correctness fallback, not a demonstrated G-C fallback. If neither construction meets G-C, record a design failure requiring a new batching or recursion construction.
215:>
216:> The current three-slot tree candidate is closed. A chain shortfall does not override its failed row gate. Reopening requires a changed candidate that passes new structural and concurrency measurements.
217:
218:**C. Complete the statement and initialization contract before key generation.**  
219:Affected text: `design.md:42`, `:54`, `:86`, `:91`; `tasks.md:67–72`.
220:
221:> The leaf derives outcome, result, selector digest and enabled-step count from constrained machine transitions. Its program digest commits to the image, layout schema, bounds and profile. Define one rule-digest encoding, including its domain, active count, padding convention and treatment of a single enabled step.
222:>
223:> Canonical initialization is established by the first-leaf relation or an explicitly authenticated initialization mechanism. Equality to a supplied init_d alone is insufficient.
224:>
225:> The final node step bound is explicit in the serialized relation identity. A bound change changes the relation version or serialized parameters and triggers the dependent key cascade.
226:
227:**D. Replace the performance baseline and adoption formula.**  
228:Affected text: `design.md:79`, `:99`, `:106–112`, `:159`.
229:
230:> Distinguish stand-in measurements from measurements using the final leaf VK. Record leaf, node and decider rows together.
231:>
232:> Use `L = ceil(H/S)`. Project total wall from setup, the slower of node service and aggregate leaf service, pipeline fill/drain, decider proving, independent verification and local call validation. Measure service times under the proposed mixed workload. Record both process and aggregate memory.
233:>
234:> At the recorded node cost, S≤2 does not meet G-C for the qualification traces. S=4 is conditional; S≥8 is the preferred candidate. k=19, tree and GPU improvements receive no projected credit without passing evidence.
235:
236:**E. Correct the formal-assurance wording.**  
237:Affected text: `design.md:85`, `:118`; tasks 2.11, 2.12, 4.2 and 5.4.
238:
239:> Composition theorems are conditional on canonical initialization, leaf soundness, digest binding and cryptographic accumulator/verifier soundness. Finite models and mutations check their modeled interfaces; they do not discharge those cryptographic premises.
240:>

