157:## 6. Open questions carried into tasks
158:
159:Q1 universal leaf k (`k_U`, task 4.1 row probe; decides S at G-A'). Q2 Jubjub-scalar VK impact per circuit (M1 regression). Q3 why one `ProofPreimage::check` of a dispatch circuit costs minutes (M3 instrumentation). Q4 prover memory for the leaf at the chosen S (4.4, cap 16 GB). Q8 (2026-11-08 (3)) what thread count produced the 95 s/step figure (2.9). Q9 where the 7,701 excess node rows are (2.3 per-gadget row report). Q10 (answered 2026-11-08, `gpu.md` §0: yes; `cudaMallocManaged` 1 GiB touched on the GPU raised the process RSS by 1.3 GB and lowered `MemAvailable` by 1.2 GB, `cudaMalloc` 1 GiB raised RSS by 1.0 GB, so a cgroup `MemoryMax` caps device allocations; F23's check re-measures it). Q11 whether the universal leaf VK's column width moves the node rows and time away from the stand-in-leaf profile (5.3 catches it; G-B exists for that reason). Q5 whether shielded.tools upgrades stagenet (owner; no dependency). Q6 the public-input limit value in 9.1.0.1 `LedgerParameters` (M1). Q7 whether `verifier.accumulate` binds its inputs with a challenge or sums them; partial answer from astra-2: at `24a1eb5a` the accumulator hashes all public encodings before deriving folding powers (`accumulator.rs:177-192,315-343`); M2 confirms at the re-pinned version and selects realization (a) or (b) of §3.2(2).

