36:| SRC-014 | U | S (owner steps per leaf) SHALL be a keyed constant of the leaf relation, chosen once at gate G-A (rule `k_U + log2(S) <= 20`, preferring S=8 at `k_U <= 17` and S=4 at `k_U = 18`) and fixed before the leaf is keyed (task 4.4), so that one key set serves every program and every step count; S=1 is the case of one enabled slot, not a different relation. When a leaf proves fewer than S enabled steps (final chunk or terminal publication), its remaining slots SHALL be disabled with identity lanes and zero contribution to `steps`; the node SHALL accept `steps` in [1, S] and refuse `steps == 0` and `steps > S`. (Amended 2026-11-08 (3); was "While S>1 is adopted ...", with S=8 an after-the-fact experiment.) | A terminal step at slot j < S-1 followed by disabled slots proves and folds; `steps == j+1`; a disabled slot with `post != pre` or a nonzero `steps` contribution is refused (row A20, mandatory once G-A fixes S; vacuous only if G-A chooses S=1). The slot semantics equal the `Leaf` of the Lean composition theorems (SRC-017, F21). | §2.3; ISSUE 5/6; owner decision 2026-11-08 (3); `order.md` §1 item 6 |
37:| SRC-015 | U | Staged throughput (added 2026-11-08 (3)). (a) After the node fixes and the k=19 cut (task 2.3), one node step SHALL prove in at most 60 s and 16 GB peak RSS at the qualification thread count, or the shortfall and its C0 phase cause SHALL be recorded and S raised at gate G-A (row A16, budget `node-k19-step`). (b) The `entry 7;` chain (6 owner steps) SHALL complete end to end (leaves, node chain or tree, decider, `verify_chain`, `validate_call`) in under 20 min, 48 GB per process, 100 GB aggregate (row A18, budget `chain-entry7`; gate G-B). (c) fact(3) (293 steps) and list123 (303 steps) SHALL each complete in under 2 h, 48 GB per process, 100 GB aggregate (rows A19, A19b, budgets `chain-fact3`, `chain-list123`; gate G-C, which blocks OP-PV-DEPLOY). Caps are seeded requirement caps (`fixed: true`), never measured-then-doubled; a shortfall is a failing row. | `budgets.json` keys `node-k19-step`, `chain-entry7`, `chain-fact3`, `chain-list123` carry `cap` with `fixed: true`; `heavy` enforces the seeded cap (task 2.0 makes `limits_for` honour a fixed cap with `measured` null); rows A16, A18, A19, A19b pass under them. | SRC-011; `order.md` §3.1, §3.3; `prover.md` §2, §6 (k19 node ESTIMATE 48-55 s, ~13 GB) |
38:| SRC-016 | U | Memory safety (added 2026-11-08 (3); E11 required). Every `heavy` process SHALL run under a kernel memory limit (cgroup v2 `MemoryMax`, `MemorySwapMax=0`, via `systemd-run --user --scope`) equal to its budget cap or, without a cap, `DW_DEFAULT_RSS_CAP` (48 GiB); no per-process cap SHALL exceed 48 GiB. A declared concurrent run (`heavy --concurrent P --aggregate-cap 100G`, E11) SHALL place its P processes in one parent scope with `MemoryMax=100G`, so the aggregate is kernel-enforced, and SHALL record per-process and aggregate peaks, P and the makespan. Preflight SHALL refuse (exit 3) when `MemAvailable` < requested cap + 20 GiB reserve or swap in use > 4 GiB. The sum of caps of every admitted heavy or gpu process across all runs SHALL not exceed 100 GiB (`queue.acquire_turn`). `cargo test` under `heavy` SHALL set `RUST_TEST_THREADS <= 4` for `mori-backend`, `mori-recursion` and `mori-ledger`, and tests that key or prove circuits above k=13 SHALL be `#[ignore]` in plain `cargo test` and run only through `scripts/qa/check-*.sh` under `heavy`. When `systemd-run` is unavailable the poll stays as the guard and the receipt records `cgroup: false`. | Factory unit tests (row F18): default cap applied, scope command built, OOM reported as `capExceeded: "rss"` from `memory.events`/exit 137, preflight refuses low `MemAvailable` and used swap, aggregate admission rule, `RUST_TEST_THREADS` injected; a 300 MB allocation under `MemoryMax=64M` exits 137 on this host (observed 2026-11-08, `order.md` §1 item 9). | SWF-004; SRC-012; E11; the 112-117 GB `mori_backend` test incident of 2026-11-08 (`order.md` §1 item 1, `prover.md` F8) |
39:| SRC-017 | U | General-purpose recursion with fixed keys and formal gates (owner decision 2026-11-08: "It has to be general purpose recursion"; "have some agents explore it with lean and quint"). The leaf, node and decider keys SHALL be independent of the program, the initial state, the step count, the fold schedule and the tree shape: one key set (leaf over the frozen inventory `R` at the keyed S, one self-recursive node, one decider, one acceptRun template) serves every committed program; S is a keyed constant; the node is self-recursive under its own key (linear chain or the uniform three-slot tree node of `tree.md` F8, in which disabled slots are the identity and the tree manifest is hash-bound); per-program, per-depth or per-level keys are refused. One general aggregation model SHALL cover both shapes (the linear chain is the degenerate tree): a Quint model `models/sherlock/quint/aggregation.qnt` (constant `TREE`, constant S) whose invariants (linkage and associativity, padding and identity neutrality, exactly-once coverage, height bounds and monotonicity, unique genesis, replay, schedule independence, program fixity, shape binding, fixed keys, liveness witness) pass with every seeded mutant caught, and Lean theorems in `clean/fork/Clean/Sherlock/Aggregation.lean` (library `SherlockSpec`, statement/axiom split) that build with zero `sorry` and whose `#print axioms` lists only the declared premises: segment soundness for every program ("the root statement implies a valid execution of the general machine for every program"), associativity of linkage, padding neutrality, exactly-once coverage, height arithmetic without wrap, decider pinning, independence from shape, depth and S. The Quint and Lean rows (F20, F21) and a council review of the design plus the formal results SHALL pass before the node constraints (2.3), the S-slot leaf (4.2) or any tree node (5.7) are implemented. | `write_relation` bytes of node and decider contain the leaf VK and k only (a program-dependent constant is a defect); F20 `quint test` passes, every mutant caught, with `TREE=false` and `TREE=true`; F21 `lake build SherlockSpec` in `clean/fork` passes with zero `sorry` and the axiom list within the premise file (`scripts/qa/check-lean-aggregation.sh`, exit 2 while the toolchain is absent); tasks 2.3, 4.2 and 5.7 list F20 and F21 in `depends`; the council review record (task 2.14) is committed. | owner decisions 2026-11-08 (3); `order.md` §1b; `tree.md` §3, §4; `prover.md` §6a, §6b; SAS-009 |
40:| SRC-018 | X | GPU backend: bit-identity and fallback (added 2026-11-08 (3); owner: "you'll have to build one in rust"; aligned 2026-11-08 with the design source `research/sherlock-speed-replan-20261108/gpu.md`). If the GPU path is enabled in the prover (the `cuda` feature of `crates/mori-gpu` built and its hooks registered by `heavy --gpu`; "the `gpu` feature" elsewhere in this change means this), its MSM (BLS12-381 G1) result SHALL equal the CPU path's (`msm_specific` over BLST `multi_exp`) **in the group**, checked on `to_affine()` and the 48-byte compressed encoding that reaches the transcript (a different projective (X, Y, Z) for the same point is not a difference), and its NTT (scalar field, midnight-curves `Fq`) result SHALL be bit-exact per element against `best_fft`, on every input including zero, one and r-1 scalars, the identity point as base and as result, duplicate bases (the P = Q case of the mixed add), projective bases with Z != 1, the signed-digit exceptions (digit -2^(c-1), top-window carry) and host- or device-resident inputs, so that proof bytes, keys, VKs and the proof format are unchanged and the stock Midnight verifier and ledger 9.1.0.1 accept the proofs; a difference SHALL fail the row (A27) and SHALL NOT be worked around by changing keys, transcripts or the decider. The backend SHALL be open source and owned in this repository as a Rust crate (`crates/mori-gpu`: Rust host, algorithm, dispatch, SRS cache, fallback, receipts and tests) with a small CUDA C++ kernel core (under about 2,000 lines) compiled by nvcc 13.4 from `build.rs` for sm_121 (plus `compute_120` PTX), using **32-bit limbs** (measured: u64 `mul`+`mulhi` runs at 0.54 T pairs/s against 7.36 T u32 `mad`/s), derived from permissively licensed sources with headers preserved (sppark Apache-2.0 templates; Yrrid/Snarkify ZPrize-2023 MIT/Apache-2.0; fallbacks ICICLE v2.8.0 MIT and ec-gpu MIT/Apache); a pure-Rust kernel route (cuda-oxide, CubeCL, Rust-CUDA) is a later port behind the same tests and hooks, not the first step (none verifies sm_121 with u64 `mul_hi` on stable Rust today). Nothing from ICICLE v3+/open-icicle CUDA backends, gnark-cuda, Nocy, Snarkify ZPrize-1B (MPL-2.0) or the WebGPU entries SHALL enter the tree, and neither sppark nor ICICLE SHALL be a crate dependency. The backend SHALL fall back to the CPU path at compile time (`cuda` off), at init time (no device, driver or toolchain; `MORI_GPU=off`) and at call time (`n < 2^MORI_GPU_MIN_K` or a kernel error), each with the same bytes and the fallback recorded in the receipt (`gpu: {arch, driver, toolkit, msm_calls, ntt_calls, fallbacks, device_bytes_peak}`; `gpu: false` when never enabled). The `midnight-proofs 0.8.3` hooks patch (two `OnceLock` registries at `msm_specific` and the `EvaluationDomain` transforms, about 60 lines, inert when unregistered) SHALL live in the separate workspace `tools/gpu-prover/` with its own `Cargo.lock` and vendored patched copy (the `tools/profile/` shape); the main workspace SHALL keep the registry crate (T0 isolation check extended to the second vendored copy, RPP-007 pattern) and `mori-gpu` SHALL NOT depend on `midnight-proofs`. Device allocations count against the process cap (measured on this host: `cudaMalloc`/`cudaMallocManaged` bytes appear in RSS and `MemAvailable`, SRC-016), so a `heavy --gpu` process SHALL run under the same cgroup caps and the receipt SHALL record `device_bytes_peak`. The backend SHALL be general purpose: any `n <= SRS size`, any `log_n <= 32`, no knowledge of the program or circuit, SRS cache keyed by content (SRC-017). | Rows F23 (G0 toolchain smoke on sm_121, done 2026-11-08: nvcc kernel and a Rust `build.rs` -> nvcc -> static lib -> zero-copy kernel, 0 mismatches), A24 (G1 source compile and G2 field and curve kernels), A25 (G3 MSM), A26 (G4 NTT), A27 (G5 integration: proof bytes identical to the CPU run under a fixed RNG seed for the `entry 7;` node, a k13 leaf below `MIN_K` and the decider, stock verify, fallback, isolation), A21 (G6 node-step measurement); each phase has the gate, kill criterion and time box of `gpu.md` §6 (tasks 2.10a-2.10f); the track opens past F23 only when gate G-A records m + q >= 0.4 and the owner funds the phases. | owner decision 2026-11-08 (3); `gpu.md` §0, F1-F6, §3, §5, §6, §7; `prover.md` F5, F6; `order.md` §1 item 8, §5.5, §7 Q4; RPP-007 |
