46:| SAS-001 | U | The assurance reporter SHALL record for every result: evidence class, dependency fingerprints (source closure, pins, keys, chain instance), semantic profile, tested bounds, command, tool versions, artifact hashes and remaining assumptions. | Schema test rejects missing fields; a finite model sample labelled as theorem or ledger acceptance is rejected. | UISEC-012; ASR-001 |
47:| SAS-002 | E | When a declared dependency (source closure, pin, key manifest, runtime, chain instance, configuration, artifact) of a result changes, the qualification checker SHALL mark the result stale until revalidated; freshness is defined by that dependency closure, not by HEAD equality, so a commit that only records evidence or factory state preserves eligibility while every declared dependency hash (including relied-on receipts) is unchanged; a HEAD-only flag may serve as an interim conservative signal but SHALL NOT be the release rule. | Change each dependency alone -> stale; unchanged-HEAD key change -> stale; a state-only commit -> still eligible. | ASR-002; `status.py:34-47,77-112`; astra-3 correction 2 |
48:| SAS-003 | X | If a negative test fails before reaching the claimed verifier stage (baseline failure, decoder refusal, synthesis error, panic, timeout, preprocessing refusal), the reporter SHALL label that stage untested and refuse constraint-rejection credit. | Inject each outcome; distinct labels; `assert_sound` requires zero panics; `qa_mutation` synthesis errors are not `Rejected`. | ASR-003; SND-007; `qa_mutation.rs:458-486,640-650` |
49:| SAS-004 | E | When a mutation campaign closes a constraint obligation, the report SHALL identify the reached verifier layer, the exact mutant, seed, case count, sampled/exhaustive status, mutation site, allowlist identity and a deliberately missing-constraint control; fresh malicious-witness proofs SHALL be included, not only public-input flips of an existing proof. | Campaign without a weakened control or without raw-witness cases is labelled partial. | ASR-004; SND-007 |
50:| SAS-005 | E | When a trace comparison closes a semantic obligation, the comparator SHALL compare complete ordered observations through a declared projection, not final values. | Intermediate preserved-field mutation with equal final result is detected; identical corruption of both producers is detected by the independent oracle. | ASR-005; UIREQ-021 |
51:| SAS-006 | S | While recursive evidence has an undischarged obligation (predecessor, accumulator, decider), the verifier SHALL refuse final-valid classification. | Altered accumulator, skipped decider, substituted key, wrong predecessor instance each rejected at the intended cryptographic boundary. | ASR-006; UISEC-010 |
52:| SAS-007 | E | When a target result qualifies a candidate, the checker SHALL match its finalized call, installed key, statement and complete effects to that candidate's manifest; it SHALL NOT select the candidate by file modification time or by any call at the address. | Receipt from another statement, contract, chain instance or runtime rejected; two candidate directories with reversed mtimes select the same candidate. | ASR-007; `check-a8.sh:7-42`; `check-a10.sh:7-24` |
53:| SAS-008 | O | Where a circuit or layout optimization is enabled, qualification SHALL retain the specified semantics and re-run affected adversarial and target checks; resource changes are reported separately. | Declared traces equal baseline; refusal set re-run. | ASR-008; UIREQ-024 |
54:| SAS-009 | E | When a release claims a formal property, the report SHALL name a checkable proof artifact, its theorem, assumptions and source closure. | Artifact or premise removed -> claim rejected; correctly labelled experimental results are not rejected. | ASR-009; UISEC-012 |
55:| SAS-010 | E | When a release admits a native rule, the inventory SHALL name evidence for invariant initialization, preservation and every fragment-composition premise. | A lane assumed canonical by one fragment, altered, is rejected by the composed leaf or excluded by a checked invariant argument. | ASR-010; `c6_dispatch_step.rs:34-38` |
56:| SAS-011 | E | When a profile, compiler, proof system, key or ledger adapter changes, qualification SHALL re-verify affected cross-layer interfaces (leaf schema, proof tag, key tag, target era) before submission. | Incompatible schema/tag/era refused before submission. | ASR-011; SRC-009 |
57:| SAS-012 | U | A release report SHALL distinguish implemented behaviour, executed evidence, proved properties and open obligations; a lower-class pass SHALL NOT close a higher-class gate. | A report generated from tasks leaves unexecuted claims open. | ASR-012; UISEC-012 |
58:| SAS-013 | U | The dispatch receipt SHALL cover every admitted rule and priority boundary by a committed partition of pre-states derived from the complete dispatch guard dependencies (control tag, site, top frame, helper kind/phase, result presence, fuel-zero, depth-zero, PROG facts, referenced values read by guards such as `equal_differ`, bounds and canonicality premises), with directed cases for every rule and boundary absent from P1-P3, every competing rule tested per class, coordinated and raw-field mutations, and fired-rule acceptance on every step; a partition known to omit a relevant guard dependency (for example the `equal_differ` value reads) SHALL NOT satisfy the receipt; a complete-dependency partition without a congruence proof SHALL be labelled a coverage heuristic, and only a checked completeness/congruence argument (one representative preserves every dispatch predicate of its class under `StepInv(pre)`) removes that label (mechanical origin alone is not enough). | Receipt JSON lists partition fields, class count, per-class rules tested, directed cases, mutations, budget key per class group, finite preprocessing scope and the heuristic/justified label; `verify_receipt` accepts it. | UIREQ-023; UISEC-001; astra-1/2/3 ISSUE 4 conditions; `c6_dispatch_step.rs:750-806,1189-1200` |
59:| SAS-014 | E | When a diagnostic uses fewer states, rules or mutations than an acceptance check, its evidence SHALL identify the reduced coverage and SHALL NOT satisfy the acceptance receipt. | Timeout or reduced run does not satisfy `verify_receipt`; inventory reports the receipt absent. | astra-3 scope clause; `uireq.py:1025-1042` |
