research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:103:- `<b>/candidate.rs`, `<b>/cell.json`, `<b>/audit.json`, `<b>/sandbox.json`, `<b>/lane/`.
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:104:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:105:Batch records: `runs/smoke/grade-batch.log` (second batch: 5 builds,
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:106:heavy run `20261109T181127Z-SKP-batch-5`, wall 8516 s, peak RSS 15.9 GB),
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:107:`runs/smoke/grader-selftest.log`. Build A of `c6_admin_publish` was graded in
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:108:an earlier batch (09:37 to 10:02) that the host killed during the next build;
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:109:its `cell.json` was then updated by hand from its receipt.
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:110:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:111:## 5. Harness defects (fix before wave 1, protocol change rule (a))
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:112:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:113:D1. Completeness uses honest steps from programs with a different layout. With
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:114:`per_rule` 2, `honest_steps` can take the second step from another program
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:115:(here fold after fact(3)). `build_all` builds one circuit per rule, from the
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:116:first honest step's layout, so the second step's statement does not fit
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:117:(`synthesis_error` for the reference too). `complete` then is false for every
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:118:build, and about half of the sampled mutants are untested. The self-test uses
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:119:`per_rule` 1 and does not see this. Fix: key circuits by (rule, program) or by
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:120:layout, and make the grade fail when the reference does not accept every honest
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:121:pair. Wave-1 components with steps in more than one program are exposed to the
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:122:same defect.
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:123:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:124:D2. The wall budget sets the coverage, and the coverage depends on the
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:125:candidate. The debug-profile grader takes 0.7 to 6.5 s per mutant. No grade
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:126:reached 4000 mutants. A smaller candidate gets more mutants in the same budget
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:127:(admin publish B: 2131 against 1186), so a wall budget confounds the primary
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:128:outcome with circuit size. The smoke used a 1800 s slot, not the 3600 s of
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:129:protocol §6. Fix options: grade with an optimized test profile; fix the count
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:130:of mutants (same seeded prefix for every build of a component) and let the
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:131:slot follow; or compare builds only on the mutant ids that every build of the
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:132:component ran.
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:133:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:134:D3. Peak RSS of the batch was 15.9 GB against the 16 GiB (17.2 GB) per-run cap,
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:135:7 % headroom. The earlier estimate was 11.5 GB.
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:136:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:137:D4. `grade-batch` writes `cell.json` records only after the whole batch, so a
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:138:killed batch leaves stale records although receipts exist.
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:139:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:140:D5. The batch reruns the grader self-test (914 s) every time. One self-test per
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:141:grader commit is enough.
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:142:
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:143:D6. Builder and skeleton lanes run `cargo check` outside `scripts/doctorwatson
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:144:heavy`. Under the host rule of 2026-11-09 (all heavy work in heavy.slice) they
research/skeleton-coding-20261108/pilot-smoke.md:145:must go through it or be shown to be light.

