53:At 20 threads, valid rerun `c0-gp-r5-t20`, step 0: **d = 0.884, m = 0.256, U = 9.77 cores** (decide C12, C14, C11). The diagnostic r4 values were d = 0.84, m = 0.24, q = 0.57, U = 8.8. m + q is above 0.4, so the GPU-track condition of G-A holds on these numbers. U is below 9 of 20 logical CPUs: one node proof does not fill the host.
54:
55:## T1(b) concurrency probe (f3)
56:
57:**f3 = 1.69 / 1.73 / 1.74** (slots 0 / 1 / 2). Solo genesis node proof at 6 threads: 75.77 s (`C0-t1b-solo-t6`, peak 16.2 GB). Three together: 128.09 / 130.68 / 131.50 s (`C0-t1b-concurrent-3`, 2026-11-09, each 16.3 GB, aggregate peak 47.7 GB, cap 60 GiB). Three concurrent proofs finish in 1.73x the solo wall, so throughput is 3 / 1.73 = 1.73x one proof at 6 threads.
58:
59:The probe is three genesis node proofs at `RAYON_NUM_THREADS=6` (`qa/sherlock/t1b-node-concurrent-3.commands`, budget `node-concurrent-3`, 20 GiB per process, 60 GiB aggregate) and the same proof solo at 6 threads. `profile-gp` has a node-only mode (`MORIARTY_GP_NODE_ONLY=1`, one stand-in leaf); the measured wall is `prove_wall_ns` of the genesis node proof in each sidecar. f3 = wall(one of three) / wall(solo).
